# Libraries that must NOT be shipped inside the AppImage: the host-provided
# allowlist. `verify.sh` also uses the reason column to print its decision table
# for the names the shipped binary mentions, so an entry here is a documented
# decision, not just a copy rule.
#
# Vendored from https://github.com/AppImage/pkg2appimage/blob/master/excludelist
# (snapshot taken 2026-10-25), restricted to the categories this project cares
# about, with deliberate local deviations documented inline.
#
# Format: `<file name>[: <reason>]`, one entry per line, matched against the
# SONAME / DT_NEEDED name (note: `bundle.sh` and `verify.sh` only look at the
# first field, so the reason may contain spaces). Lines starting with '#' and
# blank lines are ignored. Glob patterns for driver/vendor libraries live in
# `matches_driver_glob()` in excludelist.sh, which both scripts source, and are
# documented there.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. glibc and its loader. A bundled libc cannot work: the dynamic loader,
#    NSS modules, locale/gconv data and the kernel-facing bits all have to match
#    the running system, and the AppImage's whole point is to run on a *newer*
#    glibc than it was built against (see verify.sh, which enforces the 2.35
#    floor this file implies).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ld-linux.so.2: glibc loader: must be the running system's, never ours
ld-linux-x86-64.so.2: glibc loader: must be the running system's, never ours
ld-linux-aarch64.so.1: glibc loader: must be the running system's, never ours
ld-linux-armhf.so.3: glibc loader: must be the running system's, never ours
ld64.so.2: glibc loader: must be the running system's, never ours
libanl.so.1: glibc family: NSS/resolver state must match the running system
libBrokenLocale.so.1: glibc family: locale/gconv data must match the running system
libc.so.6: glibc: the core of the running system's C library
libcidn.so.1: glibc family: locale/gconv data must match the running system
libcrypt.so.1: glibc family: tied to the running system's libc
libdl.so.2: glibc family: part of the running system's libc
libm.so.6: glibc family: part of the running system's libc
libmvec.so.1: glibc family: part of the running system's libc
libnsl.so.1: glibc family: NSS/resolver state must match the running system
libnss_compat.so.2: glibc family: NSS modules must match the running system
libnss_db.so.2: glibc family: NSS modules must match the running system
libnss_dns.so.2: glibc family: NSS modules must match the running system
libnss_files.so.2: glibc family: NSS modules must match the running system
libnss_hesiod.so.2: glibc family: NSS modules must match the running system
libnss_nis.so.2: glibc family: NSS modules must match the running system
libnss_nisplus.so.2: glibc family: NSS modules must match the running system
libpthread.so.0: glibc family: part of the running system's libc
libresolv.so.2: glibc family: part of the running system's libc
librt.so.1: glibc family: part of the running system's libc
libthread_db.so.1: glibc family: part of the running system's libc
libutil.so.1: glibc family: part of the running system's libc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Graphics stack / GPU drivers. These are loaded against the *host* kernel
#    driver and the host's DRI/ICD configuration; a bundled copy either fails
#    to load or renders nothing. wgpu reaches Vulkan through dlopen anyway, so
#    none of this is a DT_NEEDED of the app (libmpv's own GL/Vulkan output is
#    compiled out).
#
#    libwayland-egl.so.1 belongs to this group even though it is not a driver:
#    it is the `wl_egl_window` glue shipped by Mesa, and it has to match the
#    EGL implementation the host resolves, so it is host-provided like libEGL.
#
#    Note what is deliberately NOT here:
#      * libva.so.2 and libva-x11/wayland ARE bundled (they are the API library,
#        a hard DT_NEEDED of libmpv once -Dvaapi is on; the vendor driver they
#        dlopen stays on the host). libva is the *other* library a host vendor
#        user-space binds to: a host Mesa VA-API driver links libva.so.2, so the
#        same symbol-drift caveat as section 3 applies to it, and it is accepted
#        (the alternative is shipping no VA-API support at all). Watch for a host
#        driver needing a newer VA_API_* version than our copy exports -- the
#        plugin-host class is therefore *not* fully closed,
#      * libX11/libxcb/libwayland-client are bundled too so the app never
#        depends on the host having them at a compatible version,
#      * libpulse.so.0 is bundled. It is *not* immune to section 3's rule: the
#        host's ALSA pulse plugin (libasound_module_pcm_pulse.so) has a hard
#        DT_NEEDED on libpulse.so.0, so it binds our copy. It stays bundled
#        because it is a hard DT_NEEDED of libmpv (-Dpulse=enabled) and because
#        loading the current distributions' plugin against it showed no symbol
#        drift (no "version `PULSE_...' not found"). It is the one plugin-host
#        exception being watched: if a host plugin ever asks for a newer PULSE_*
#        version than our copy exports, it moves to section 3,
#      * libgcc_s.so.1 is bundled (see README): libavcodec's `_Unwind_*` usage
#        needs a recent enough one.
#    The plugin hosts that must stay on the host are in section 3.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
libGL.so.1: GPU driver entry point: must match the host kernel driver and GPU
libEGL.so.1: EGL entry point: must match the host's EGL implementation
libGLX.so.0: GLVND: dispatches to the host driver
libGLdispatch.so.0: GLVND: dispatches to the host driver
libOpenGL.so.0: GLVND: dispatches to the host driver
libglapi.so.0: Mesa internal: must match the host Mesa
libwayland-egl.so.1: Mesa's wl_egl_window glue: must match the host EGL
libwayland-egl.so: dev-link name of libwayland-egl.so.1 (host-provided, see above)
libdrm_amdgpu.so.1: driver-facing libdrm: must match the host kernel driver
libdrm_intel.so.1: driver-facing libdrm: must match the host kernel driver
libdrm_nouveau.so.2: driver-facing libdrm: must match the host kernel driver
libdrm_radeon.so.1: driver-facing libdrm: must match the host kernel driver
libgbm.so.1: buffer allocation: must match the host kernel driver
libvulkan.so.1: Vulkan loader: enumerates the host's ICDs
libvulkan_lvp.so: Mesa's lavapipe ICD: a driver, so host-provided

# Optional vendor user-space the bundled libva probes for at runtime (dlopen'd,
# absent on most systems, and libva falls back cleanly when the dlopen fails).
# They are the vendor's own driver code, so they are host-provided like every
# other entry in this section -- never bundled, never required.
libatiadlxx.so: AMD ADL userspace probed by libva-x11: vendor driver, optional
libwayland-emgd.so.1: NVIDIA EGLStream Wayland userspace probed by libva-wayland: vendor driver, optional

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Plugin hosts and system interfaces. These are libraries the *host* dlopens
#    plugins into our process for, and a plugin binds to them BY SONAME. Once
#    the bundled (older) copy is loaded under that SONAME, the host plugin
#    binds to it and dies on a versioned symbol it needs. Measured against the
#    real payload of this branch:
#
#      /usr/lib/alsa-lib/libasound_module_pcm_pulse.so
#        -> /tmp/fa/usr/lib/libasound.so.2: version `ALSA_1.2.15' not found
#      /usr/lib/dri/radeonsi_drv_video.so
#        -> /tmp/fa/usr/lib/libstdc++.so.6: version `GLIBCXX_3.4.32' not found
#           (required by /usr/lib/libSPIRV-Tools.so)
#
#    Consequence: rodio -> cpal -> ALSA "default" -> the host's pulse/pipewire
#    plugin failed to load, so audio was silently dead on current distributions,
#    and VA-API drivers degenerated or failed. Both were bundled before that
#    measurement; they are host-provided now.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
libasound.so.2: ALSA plugin host: host plugins (module_pcm_pulse) bind ALSA_* from the host copy
libstdc++.so.6: C++ plugin host: stacked plugins (libSPIRV-Tools) need the host's GLIBCXX_*
libdrm.so.2: system interface: host Mesa/VA-API drivers link it and may need newer drm* symbols
